@blessyou5081 Oh jeesh, are you going to justify any of that? You’re conflating societal survival with individual happiness. Yes, societies require reproduction on scale, that does not therefore mean women’s personal fulfillment hinges on marriage or children. Thats just statistically wrong, and fallacious (category error). 

Really work stress, men also experience job dissatisfaction and stress; pretending this is uniquely punishing to women ignores actual data and structural factors such as housing costs, wage stagnation, debt, and social media pressure, none of which are linked to bearing children. Always seems the case, that these arguments ignore men to say things about women, and what women ought to do, just to put diminish both sexes. 

